# What Cloudflare must NOT publish.
#
# Wrangler uploads from the working tree, not from git, so .gitignore does
# not apply here — gas-backend.gs.js is ignored by git but sits on disk and
# would otherwise be served publicly. Everything the running app needs is
# index.html, manifest.json, moved.html, boot.js, data.js, compiled/, vendor/
# and icons/. Anything not on that list belongs below.
#
# boot.js, compiled/ and vendor/ must never be listed: without boot.js the app
# silently runs in LOCAL MOCK MODE, without the other two it is a blank page.
# test/verify-build-shells.cjs fails if any of them is excluded here.
#
# The six .jsx sources are no longer loaded by the shells (2026-09-17 build
# step) but stay published for that release: a browser still holding the
# previous index.html asks for them until it revalidates. Exclude them in a
# later release, not this one.

.git/
.claude/
.gitignore
.gitleaksignore
.gitleaks.toml
.graphifyignore
.github/
.serena/
_config.yml
.gitattributes

# Ledgers, reviews and specs — internal, and SECURITY_CHECKLIST.md especially
*.md

# Backend source. Served by Google Apps Script, never by Cloudflare.
gas-backend.gs
gas-backend.gs.js

# Tooling output and dev-only trees
# .wrangler/ is scaffolding wrangler creates inside this directory during a
# deploy; without this line its no-op-worker stub is uploaded and served.
.wrangler/
docs/
graphify-out/
test/
node_modules/
# The build (tools/build.mjs, its package.json and lockfile). Runs on a
# developer machine and in CI, never on a host; its output is committed.
tools/

# Center Point staging entry (PR #57). Synthetic, and served only by CP's own
# server from `neofeedDirectory` — never by the clinical NeoFeed domain.
center-point/

# NOTE: wrangler.jsonc cannot be listed here. Wrangler force-includes its own
# config file when it sits inside the assets directory, so it IS served at
# /wrangler.jsonc. Verified 2026-08-23: adding it here changes nothing, and
# moving it out of the repo is the only thing that hides it. It holds no
# secrets (name, compatibility_date, assets directory), so it is left public
# rather than moved somewhere Workers Builds would not find it.

# The local editing copy of index.html, byte-identical to it. Publishing a
# second copy of the whole app at a second URL only creates a stale twin.
NeoFeed.html
